A1b  send while busy
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  session 617825c8-0a5a-4e52-bd90-8dea5475cc5a
  driver           opencode-server (family server)
  CONTROL          phase reached 'working': true (2627ms)
  second send      {"ok":true,"queued":true,"disposition":"queued"}
  disposition      "queued"
  position in the send's return: (absent)
  position in any socket frame:  (no frame carried one)
  frames seen      hostMetricsChanged=2 sessionAgentStateChanged=2 welcome=1 machinesChanged=1 approvalsChanged=1 attached=1 presenceRoomState=1 presenceRoomDelta=1 transcriptDelta=1
  after reload     sessions.queue -> null
  waiting for the busy turn to finish and the queued one to run …
  busy turn ended  true (BUSY-NYNZPT)
  queued delivered true (QUEUED-00ZYJF)

  A1b PARTIAL
      queued with position: yes (queued, position not reported)
      survived a real reload (socket closed and reopened): true
      delivered when idle: true
      PARTIAL, not PASS: the message was NOT lost — it reported itself as
      queued, survived the reload and ran when the session went idle — but NO
      POSITION reached the caller, on the return or on any socket frame.
      The product does compute one (runtime-gateway.ts:49, 1-based, read off
      the real queue depth); sessions.sendText narrows its reply to four
      pinned keys (command-plane.ts:459) and position is not among them, and
      the receipt that does carry it travels the MESSAGE path, not the chat
      one. So a chat UI cannot show a person where they are in a queue.

